                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This isn’t one of the most exciting games on Steam imo. WireNet is like any bullet hell game, but in a 2D world consisted of green visuals over a black BG. The cast of enemies and entire platform also ranges from 8-bit quality consisting namely of more more than circles or squares. There’s no guide, no music and the only audio is the annoying spam of bullets that you can shoot towards at one direction. On the note of directions, it’s also pretty BS that the bullets the enemies fire can go a full 360 degrees, while our aim is limited to literally four directions (AWSD keys). You have the HP on the top left, and AMP and DEF on the bottom of the screen, as well as other labels that aren’t explained. I’m not sure why they are there either. \n\nI barely finished level 1 before stopping completely. The idea behind this game is bland and generic. Some enemies become repetitive, too. The overall design of the game is left at a basic and unpolished state as it is. There are better bullet hell games than WireNet on Steam to play.",
